 "title": "Register of Deeds - Platte County Nebraska",
 "text": "Register of Deeds - Platte County Nebraska\nAbout\nCalendar\nOffices\nAdult Diversion\nAssessor\nAttorney\nBoard of Supervisors\nCASA\nChild Support Division\nCivil Rights Coordinator\nCounty Clerk\nCounty Court\nDistrict Court\nDMV\nEmergency Management\nElection Commission\nExtension Office\nFloodplain Administrator\nGeneral Assistance\nHighway Department\nJuvenile Diversion\nProbation\nPlanning & Zoning\nPublic Defender\nSheriff’s Office\nRegister of Deeds\nTreasurer\nVisitors Bureau\nVeterans’ Services\nVictim Assistance\nWeed Control Authority\nExternal Links\nPassports\nSelect Page\nRegister of Deeds\nContact\nSigrid Parker\nRegister of Deeds\nDiane Kapels\nDeputy\nLocation\nPlatte County Courthouse\nFirst floor, east side\nAddress\n2610 14th Street\nColumbus, NE 68601\nPhone : 402-563-4911\nFax: 402-563-9173\nHours\n8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.\nMonday – Friday\nLinks\nFee Sheet\nGeographical Information System (GIS)\nFill-In Form 521\nNebraska Document Stamp\nTax Calculation Example\nDocumentary Stamp Tax Exemption Chart\nNebraska Deeds Online\nDocument Cover Sheet\nNebraska Department of Revenue – Property Assessment Division\nNebraska Secretary of State – UCC Forms\nContact\nYour name\nYour email\nSubject\nYour message (optional)\nSubmit\nThe mission of the Platte County Register of Deeds is to record all documents promptly and efficiently, preserving them for the future. Our office shall be committed to providing information and serving the public in an efficient, courteous, and economical manner.\nThe Register of Deeds Department is responsible for recording and maintaining all transactions having to do with real property. The duties of the office are to record the documents presented at the time of delivery, proofread them, and index them accordingly. Documents received in the Register of Deeds Department include, but are not limited to, various deeds, plats, deeds of trust, death certificates, and state and federal tax liens. The Register of Deeds Department makes hard copies and scans documents and processes them for use.\nPlatte County currently has certain records available online. You can obtain data by searching grantor/grantee or by legal description and print copies free of charge. We currently have data and documents available to view or print from February 1, 2005 to the present. The website is nebraskadeedsonline.us .\nLooking for documents recorded prior to Nebraska Deeds Online? Click here to access archived records.\n🏡 Exciting News from the Platte County Register of Deeds!\nWe are thrilled to announce the launch of our Property Fraud Alert Service – a FREE and proactive way to protect your most valuable asset: your property.\nWith this service, you’ll receive alerts if someone tries to record a document in your name, giving you peace of mind and an extra layer of protection.\n🔒 Sign up today and safeguard your property!\nFor more information click here .\nTo sign up for Property Fraud Alert click here\nDocumentary Stamp Tax Rate History\nNovember 18, 1965 – September 5, 1985\n$0.55 per each $500 of valute of $1.10 per $1,000 of value\nSeptember 6, 1985 – December 31, 1992\n$1.50 per each $1,000 of value\nJanuary 1, 1993 – June 30, 2005\n$1.75 per each $1,000 of value\nJuly 1, 2005 – September 2, 2025\n$2.25 per each $1,000 of value\nSeptember 3, 2025 – July 17, 2026\n$2.32 per each $1,000 of value\nJuly 18, 2026 – December 31, 2031\n$3.32 per each $1,000 of value\nNote: In 1965, Nebraska adopted a documentary stamp tax act to become law upon repeal of the federal documentary stamp act. The Nebraska Documentary Stamp Act became effective January 1, 1968. The federal rate at the time of repeal was $0.55 per each $500.00 of value or fraction thereof.\nCourthouse\nAddress\n2610 14th Street\nColumbus, NE 68601\nHours\n8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m.\nMonday – Friday\nOther\nPrivacy Policy\nFollow\nFollow\nen\nArabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Italian Portuguese Russian Spanish",
